{
    "id": "meals_dispositions",
    "title": "Dispositions",
    "est_minutes": 16,
    "summary": "The ten codes, and the edge cases that get miscoded.",
    "badge": {
        "id": "badge_meals_dispositions",
        "name": "Clean Coder",
        "icon": "🗂️"
    },
    "lessons": [
        {
            "id": "m6_1",
            "title": "The ten codes",
            "est_minutes": 5,
            "blocks": [
                {
                    "type": "text",
                    "html": "<table><tr><th>Code</th><th>Use when</th></tr><tr><td><strong>Transfer</strong></td><td>The screener took the call and the handoff was completed</td></tr><tr><td><strong>DQ</strong></td><td>No Medicaid, copays, a non-qualifying plan, Medicare only, or outside the five boroughs</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Not Interested</strong></td><td>They decline, or hang up after acknowledging who they are</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Call Back</strong></td><td>They ask to be called back</td></tr><tr><td><strong>DNC</strong></td><td>Stop calling, remove me, or a threat</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Hung-Up Transfer</strong></td><td>They hang up after the transfer starts</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Dead Air</strong></td><td>No response at all</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Answering Machine</strong></td><td>Voicemail — leave no message</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Wrong Number</strong></td><td>The person asked for isn't there</td></tr><tr><td><strong>No English</strong></td><td>Can't continue in English</td></tr></table>"
                },
                {
                    "type": "check",
                    "question": "A consumer says “yes, that's me” then hangs up. Code?",
                    "choices": [
                        "Wrong Number",
                        "Not Interested",
                        "Dead Air",
                        "Hung-Up Transfer"
                    ],
                    "answer_index": 1,
                    "explanation": "They acknowledged, so it's Not Interested."
                }
            ]
        },
        {
            "id": "m6_2",
            "title": "DQ is the one that matters",
            "est_minutes": 5,
            "blocks": [
                {
                    "type": "text",
                    "html": "<p>DQ is the code that protects the campaign. Five reasons: no Medicaid, copays at the doctor, a plan that isn't on the list, Medicare only, or living outside the five boroughs.</p>"
                },
                {
                    "type": "callout",
                    "tone": "warning",
                    "title": "38 disqualified consumers were transferred anyway",
                    "html": "<p>Out of 169 who should have been DQ'd, 99 were caught. The rest were sent to a screener who couldn't help them — wasting the screener's time and billing a transfer that shouldn't exist.</p>"
                },
                {
                    "type": "text",
                    "html": "<p>Read the DQ line, code it DQ, move to the next call. It takes ten seconds and it's a correct outcome.</p>"
                },
                {
                    "type": "check",
                    "question": "Someone is in Yonkers. Code?",
                    "choices": [
                        "Transfer — it's near NYC",
                        "Call Back",
                        "DQ — outside the five boroughs",
                        "Wrong Number"
                    ],
                    "answer_index": 2,
                    "explanation": "Only the five boroughs qualify."
                }
            ]
        },
        {
            "id": "m6_3",
            "title": "The ones that get mixed up",
            "est_minutes": 4,
            "blocks": [
                {
                    "type": "text",
                    "html": "<p><strong>Not Interested vs Dead Air:</strong> did they acknowledge? If they said anything that showed they were there, it's Not Interested. Silence throughout is Dead Air.</p>"
                },
                {
                    "type": "text",
                    "html": "<p><strong>Not Interested vs Hung-Up Transfer:</strong> did you start the transfer? Before — Not Interested. After — Hung-Up Transfer.</p>"
                },
                {
                    "type": "text",
                    "html": "<p><strong>Call Back vs Not Interested:</strong> “call me back” during a brush-off that you then rebut and lose is Not Interested. An actual request to be called at a specific time is a Call Back.</p>"
                },
                {
                    "type": "callout",
                    "tone": "tip",
                    "title": "Code what happened",
                    "html": "<p>Not what you hoped happened. Miscoding patterns get noticed, and on this campaign they've cost people their seats.</p>"
                },
                {
                    "type": "check",
                    "question": "You hit transfer, the screener's line rings, and the consumer hangs up. Code?",
                    "choices": [
                        "Hung-Up Transfer",
                        "Not Interested",
                        "Dead Air",
                        "Conference Ending"
                    ],
                    "answer_index": 0,
                    "explanation": "After the transfer starts, it's a Hung-Up Transfer."
                }
            ]
        },
        {
            "id": "m6_4",
            "title": "Voicemail and wrong numbers",
            "est_minutes": 2,
            "blocks": [
                {
                    "type": "text",
                    "html": "<p><strong>Answering Machine:</strong> you reach voicemail. <strong>Do not leave a message.</strong></p><p><strong>Wrong Number:</strong> the person you asked for isn't at this number. Don't pitch whoever answered — they aren't the lead and they haven't consented to anything.</p>"
                },
                {
                    "type": "check",
                    "question": "Someone else answers and says the person you asked for doesn't live there. What do you do?",
                    "choices": [
                        "Ask for a forwarding number",
                        "Code Wrong Number and move on",
                        "Code Not Interested",
                        "Pitch them instead"
                    ],
                    "answer_index": 1,
                    "explanation": "They're not your lead."
                }
            ]
        }
    ],
